  "text": " Calder looked at him. Board doesn't say he was wrong, she said. The board says it doesn't know. And that a country that doesn't know shouldn't be one engine while it finds out. That's the works reading. It's the only one in this hall that isn't a reading of what's coming. It's a reading of what to do in the meantime. She folded her hands. Write that the board heard Mr. Holden, and that it doesn't say he was wrong, and that it doesn't say he was right, and that it orders the banks on their own counts anyway, because a fitter's rule is all it's got. The heavy board member pushed his spectacles up onto his forehead.",
